    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "FAQs"
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "1. Do teeth braces hurt all the time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "No. Braces hurt mainly during the first few days and after adjustments. The pain fades as your mouth adjusts."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "2. What can I do to stop the braces' pain immediately?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Use ice packs, take pain relievers, apply orthodontic wax, and rinse with salt water. These give quick relief."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "3. Can I eat regular food with braces?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When it hurts, stick to soft foods like khichdi and bananas. Avoid crunchy or hard items during sore days."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "4. Are there long-term pain relief options?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Yes. Interventional Radiology offers non-surgical pain solutions during orthodontic treatment. Ask your orthodontist."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "5. When should I worry about braces pain?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If the pain is severe, doesn't go away, or you see swelling or a broken bracket, visit your orthodontist fast."
    }
